IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ha-types`
IMPORT `ha-pay`
IMPORT `ha-annual`
IMPORT `ha-public`
IMPORT `ha-leave`
IMPORT `ha-enforcement`
IMPORT `ha-goal`

-- Independent tests for the Holidays Act 2003 (NZ) encoding.
-- Every expected value comes from independent-expectations.md, written from
-- the statute before the encoding was read. E-nnn tags cite that file.
-- A failing assertion is a finding: expected values are never changed to
-- match the encoding.

§ `Helpers`

GIVEN owp IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Weekly pay facts`
wkpay owp MEANS `Weekly pay facts` OF TRUE, owp, 0, 0, NOTHING, 0, 0, NOTHING

GIVEN rdp IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Daily pay facts`
dpay rdp MEANS `Daily pay facts` OF TRUE, rdp, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, 52000, 260

GIVEN yr IS A NUMBER, mat IS A DATE, ann IS A DATE, wd IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A `Calendar inputs`
calx yr mat ann wd MEANS `Calendar inputs` OF yr, mat, ann, wd

monfri MEANS LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5
monsat MEANS LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6
sunfri MEANS LIST 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5
allweek MEANS LIST 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6

cal2022 MEANS calx 2022 (Date 24 6 2022) (Date 24 1 2022) monfri
cal2023 MEANS calx 2023 (Date 14 7 2023) (Date 23 1 2023) monfri
cal2024 MEANS calx 2024 (Date 28 6 2024) (Date 22 1 2024) monfri
cal2025 MEANS calx 2025 (Date 20 6 2025) (Date 20 1 2025) monfri
cal2026 MEANS calx 2026 (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 19 1 2026) monfri
cal2027 MEANS calx 2027 (Date 25 6 2027) (Date 18 1 2027) monfri
cal2028 MEANS calx 2028 (Date 14 7 2028) (Date 24 1 2028) monfri
cal2038 MEANS calx 2038 (Date 25 6 2038) (Date 25 1 2038) monfri
cal2026sat MEANS calx 2026 (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 19 1 2026) monsat
cal2027sat MEANS calx 2027 (Date 25 6 2027) (Date 18 1 2027) monsat
cal2027sun MEANS calx 2027 (Date 25 6 2027) (Date 18 1 2027) sunfri
cal2027all MEANS calx 2027 (Date 25 6 2027) (Date 18 1 2027) allweek

GIVEN ow IS A BOOLEAN, wk IS A BOOLEAN, rq IS A BOOLEAN, rs IS A `Reason for not working`, onlyph IS A BOOLEAN, oc IS AN `On call`, por IS A NUMBER, pen IS A NUMBER, porr IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Public holiday worked or not`
phx ow wk rq rs onlyph oc por pen porr MEANS `Public holiday worked or not` OF (Date 25 12 2025), ow, wk, rq, rs, onlyph, oc, (dpay 200), por, pen, porr

GIVEN st IS A DATE
GIVETH A Service
svc st MEANS Service OF st, NOTHING, FALSE

GIVEN k IS A `Leave kind`, lb IS A DATE, st IS A DATE, ds IS A NUMBER, lft IS A NUMBER, adv IS A BOOLEAN, ws IS A `Whose sickness`, acc IS A NUMBER, bs IS A LIST OF Bereavement
GIVETH A Leave
lv k lb st ds lft adv ws acc bs MEANS Leave OF k, lb, (svc st), ds, lft, adv, ws, bs, (`Family violence facts` OF TRUE, FALSE), (dpay 200), acc, FALSE

GIVEN begins IS A DATE, wks IS A NUMBER, adv IS A BOOLEAN, st IS A DATE, owp IS A NUMBER, lpe IS A DATE, gross IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Annual holiday`
ahol begins wks adv st owp lpe gross MEANS `Annual holiday` OF begins, wks, adv, st, (wkpay owp), lpe, gross, EMPTY

GIVEN ent IS A BOOLEAN, wks IS A NUMBER, owp IS A NUMBER, g12 IS A NUMBER, gs IS A NUMBER, adv IS A NUMBER, pg IS A NUMBER, phs IS A NUMBER, ahs IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `End of employment`
eoe ent wks owp g12 gs adv pg phs ahs MEANS `End of employment` OF (Date 19 12 2025), (Date 1 3 2024), ent, wks, (wkpay owp), g12, EMPTY, gs, adv, pg, phs, ahs, (dpay 200)

-- [Ported by the encoder: Payout request gained the entitlement not taken (4 weeks here) and the absences list (none).]
GIVEN wr IS A BOOLEAN, req IS A NUMBER, already IS A NUMBER, pol IS A BOOLEAN, agr IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Payout request`
pr wr req already pol agr MEANS `Payout request` OF wr, req, already, pol, agr, (wkpay 1000), 57200, 4, EMPTY

-- [Ported by the encoder: Closedown gained the absences list (none).]
GIVEN nt IS A DATE, other IS A BOOLEAN, ent IS A BOOLEAN, wks IS A NUMBER, avail IS A NUMBER, agr IS A BOOLEAN, gs IS A NUMBER, adv IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Closedown
cd nt other ent wks avail agr gs adv MEANS Closedown OF (Date 22 12 2025), nt, other, ent, wks, avail, agr, (wkpay 1000), 52000, gs, adv, 0, EMPTY

GIVEN tk IS A DATE, agr IS A BOOLEAN, owd IS A BOOLEAN, whole IS A BOOLEAN, isph IS A BOOLEAN, nt IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH AN `Alternative holiday`
alth tk agr owd whole isph nt MEANS `Alternative holiday` OF tk, agr, owd, whole, isph, nt, (dpay 200)

GIVEN ab IS A `Kind of absence`, len IS A NUMBER, agr IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Absence
absx ab len agr MEANS Absence OF ab, len, agr

GIVEN k IS A `Payment kind`, amt IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Payment
pay k amt MEANS Payment OF k, amt

§ `1. Pay measures`

-- E-001 OWP under s 8(1) with regular commission, regular overtime and board
#ASSERT `the ordinary weekly pay` (`Weekly pay facts` OF TRUE, 1000, 200, 100, (JUST (`Board or lodgings` OF 50, FALSE, FALSE)), 0, 0, NOTHING) EQUALS 1350
-- E-002 commission not regular: not an input
#ASSERT `the ordinary weekly pay` (`Weekly pay facts` OF TRUE, 1000, 0, 100, (JUST (`Board or lodgings` OF 50, FALSE, FALSE)), 0, 0, NOTHING) EQUALS 1150
-- E-004 s 8(2) (a - b) / c
#ASSERT `the ordinary weekly pay` (`Weekly pay facts` OF FALSE, 0, 0, 0, NOTHING, 4800, 400, NOTHING) EQUALS 1100
-- E-005 s 8(2) monthly pay period, c is still 4
#ASSERT `the ordinary weekly pay` (`Weekly pay facts` OF FALSE, 0, 0, 0, NOTHING, 4333, 0, NOTHING) EQUALS 1083.25
-- E-006
#ASSERT `the ordinary weekly pay` (`Weekly pay facts` OF FALSE, 0, 0, 0, NOTHING, 4000, 0, NOTHING) EQUALS 1000
-- E-007 s 8(3) special rate higher
#ASSERT `the ordinary weekly pay` (`Weekly pay facts` OF FALSE, 0, 0, 0, NOTHING, 4800, 400, (JUST 1200)) EQUALS 1200
-- E-008 s 8(3) special rate lower is ineffective
#ASSERT `the ordinary weekly pay` (`Weekly pay facts` OF FALSE, 0, 0, 0, NOTHING, 4800, 400, (JUST 1000)) EQUALS 1100
-- E-009 special rate equal
#ASSERT `the ordinary weekly pay` (`Weekly pay facts` OF FALSE, 0, 0, 0, NOTHING, 4800, 400, (JUST 1100)) EQUALS 1100
-- E-010 RDP s 9(1)
#ASSERT `the relevant daily pay` (`Daily pay facts` OF TRUE, 280, (JUST (`Board or lodgings` OF 10, FALSE, FALSE)), NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0) EQUALS 290
-- E-012 s 9(1A) special rate higher / lower
#ASSERT `the relevant daily pay` (`Daily pay facts` OF TRUE, 280, (JUST (`Board or lodgings` OF 10, FALSE, FALSE)), (JUST 300), FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0) EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `the relevant daily pay` (`Daily pay facts` OF TRUE, 280, (JUST (`Board or lodgings` OF 10, FALSE, FALSE)), (JUST 250), FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0) EQUALS 290
-- E-014 ADP s 9A(2)
#ASSERT `the average daily pay` (`Daily pay facts` OF FALSE, 0, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, 52000, 260) EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `the daily pay` (`Daily pay facts` OF FALSE, 0, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, 52000, 260) EQUALS 200
-- E-015
#ASSERT `the average daily pay` (`Daily pay facts` OF FALSE, 0, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, 45000, 225) EQUALS 200
-- E-016 when ADP may be used, s 9A(1)
#ASSERT `the employer may use average daily pay` (`Daily pay facts` OF TRUE, 180, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, TRUE, 52000, 260) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the employer may use average daily pay` (`Daily pay facts` OF TRUE, 180, NOTHING, NOTHING, TRUE, TRUE, 52000, 260) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the employer may use average daily pay` (`Daily pay facts` OF FALSE, 180, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, 52000, 260) EQUALS TRUE
-- E-016 neither limb: RDP is used even if the employer prefers ADP
#ASSERT `the daily pay` (`Daily pay facts` OF TRUE, 180, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, TRUE, 52000, 260) EQUALS 180
#ASSERT `the daily pay` (`Daily pay facts` OF TRUE, 180, NOTHING, NOTHING, TRUE, TRUE, 52000, 260) EQUALS 200
-- E-017 whole or part days
#ASSERT `the average daily pay` (`Daily pay facts` OF FALSE, 0, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, 42000, 210) EQUALS 200
-- E-018 board agreed included; E-019 overnight away excluded; E-020 special circumstances excluded
#ASSERT `the ordinary weekly pay` (`Weekly pay facts` OF TRUE, 1000, 0, 0, (JUST (`Board or lodgings` OF 60, FALSE, FALSE)), 0, 0, NOTHING) EQUALS 1060
#ASSERT `the ordinary weekly pay` (`Weekly pay facts` OF TRUE, 1000, 0, 0, (JUST (`Board or lodgings` OF 60, TRUE, FALSE)), 0, 0, NOTHING) EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the relevant daily pay` (`Daily pay facts` OF TRUE, 200, (JUST (`Board or lodgings` OF 10, FALSE, TRUE)), NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0) EQUALS 200
-- E-022 gross earnings s 14 and s 10A
#ASSERT `the gross earnings in` (LIST (pay `(a)(i) salary or wages` 50000), (pay `(a)(ii) an allowance, other than a non-taxable reimbursement of actual costs` 2000), (pay `(a)(iii) pay for a holiday or leave taken in the period` 4000), (pay `(a)(iv) a productivity or incentive-based payment` 3000), (pay `(a)(v) a payment for overtime` 1000), (pay `(a)(vi) the cash value of board or lodgings agreed or determined under s 10` 500), (pay `(a)(vii) first week compensation under s 97 of the Accident Compensation Act 2001` 800), (pay `s 10A(a) a payment under s 14 of the Home and Community Support Settlement Act 2016` 700), (pay `(b)(i) a discretionary payment` 1000), (pay `(b)(ii) weekly compensation under the Accident Compensation Act 2001` 2000), (pay `(b)(iii) a payment for absence on volunteers leave` 300), (pay `(c)(i) a reimbursement of actual costs` 400), (pay `(c)(ii) a reimbursement of a reasonably assessed amount of costs` 200), (pay `(c)(iii) an employer contribution to a superannuation scheme` 1500), (pay `(c)(iv) a payment for annual holidays paid out under s 28B` 900), (pay `s 10A(b) a payment under s 19 of the Home and Community Support Settlement Act 2016` 250)) EQUALS 62000
-- E-024 AWE
#ASSERT `the average weekly earnings over 12 months, gross` 52000 `, absences` EMPTY EQUALS 1000
-- E-025 exactly 1 week agreed: divisor 52
#ASSERT `the divisor for 12 months, after s 16(3), given` (LIST (absx `other unpaid leave` 7 TRUE)) EQUALS 52
-- E-026 3 weeks agreed: divisor 50; AWE 1000 on 50000
#ASSERT `the divisor for 12 months, after s 16(3), given` (LIST (absx `other unpaid leave` 21 TRUE)) EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `the average weekly earnings over 12 months, gross` 50000 `, absences` (LIST (absx `other unpaid leave` 21 TRUE)) EQUALS 1000
-- E-027 1 week and 1 day: divisor 51
#ASSERT `the divisor for 12 months, after s 16(3), given` (LIST (absx `other unpaid leave` 8 TRUE)) EQUALS 51
-- E-028 about 2.5 weeks: divisor 50
#ASSERT `the divisor for 12 months, after s 16(3), given` (LIST (absx `other unpaid leave` 18 TRUE)) EQUALS 50
-- E-026b unpaid sick leave does not reduce the divisor
#ASSERT `the divisor for 12 months, after s 16(3), given` (LIST (absx `(a)(v) unpaid sick, bereavement or family violence leave` 21 FALSE)) EQUALS 52

§ `2. Annual holidays`

-- E-030 entitlement date
#ASSERT `the day the employee becomes entitled to annual holidays, 12 months from` (Date 1 3 2024) `, absences` EMPTY EQUALS Date 1 3 2025
-- E-031 second entitlement
#ASSERT `the day the employee becomes entitled to annual holidays, 12 months from` (Date 1 3 2025) `, absences` EMPTY EQUALS Date 1 3 2026
-- E-032
#ASSERT `the annual holidays entitlement in weeks` EQUALS 4
-- E-033 other unpaid leave of exactly 1 week counts
#ASSERT `the day the employee becomes entitled to annual holidays, 12 months from` (Date 1 3 2024) `, absences` (LIST (absx `other unpaid leave` 7 FALSE)) EQUALS Date 1 3 2025
-- E-034 8 days not agreed: pushed back 8 days
#ASSERT `the day the employee becomes entitled to annual holidays, 12 months from` (Date 1 3 2024) `, absences` (LIST (absx `other unpaid leave` 8 FALSE)) EQUALS Date 9 3 2025
-- E-035 8 days agreed: counts
#ASSERT `the day the employee becomes entitled to annual holidays, 12 months from` (Date 1 3 2024) `, absences` (LIST (absx `other unpaid leave` 8 TRUE)) EQUALS Date 1 3 2025
-- E-036 to E-039 included absences
#ASSERT `the day the employee becomes entitled to annual holidays, 12 months from` (Date 1 3 2024) `, absences` (LIST (absx `(a)(v) unpaid sick, bereavement or family violence leave` 21 FALSE)) EQUALS Date 1 3 2025
#ASSERT `the day the employee becomes entitled to annual holidays, 12 months from` (Date 1 3 2024) `, absences` (LIST (absx `(a)(ii) parental leave` 180 FALSE)) EQUALS Date 1 3 2025
#ASSERT `the day the employee becomes entitled to annual holidays, 12 months from` (Date 1 3 2024) `, absences` (LIST (absx `(a)(iv) receiving weekly compensation under the Accident Compensation Act 2001` 60 FALSE)) EQUALS Date 1 3 2025
#ASSERT `the day the employee becomes entitled to annual holidays, 12 months from` (Date 1 3 2024) `, absences` (LIST (absx `(a)(iii) volunteers leave` 10 FALSE)) EQUALS Date 1 3 2025
-- E-041 s 18(1)
#ASSERT `the last day by which the employer must allow the holidays, entitlement arising` (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS Date 1 3 2026
-- E-044 s 19: notice 1 Dec, start 15 Dec = 14 days: valid
#ASSERT `the employer may require annual holidays from` (Date 15 12 2025) `, no agreement under s 18(3):` TRUE `, s 32 applies:` FALSE `, notice on` (Date 1 12 2025) EQUALS TRUE
-- E-045 13 days: invalid
#ASSERT `the employer may require annual holidays from` (Date 14 12 2025) `, no agreement under s 18(3):` TRUE `, s 32 applies:` FALSE `, notice on` (Date 1 12 2025) EQUALS FALSE
-- E-046 agreement reached and no closedown: no power to require
#ASSERT `the employer may require annual holidays from` (Date 31 12 2025) `, no agreement under s 18(3):` FALSE `, s 32 applies:` FALSE `, notice on` (Date 1 12 2025) EQUALS FALSE
-- E-050 s 21: 2 weeks at max(1000, 1100)
#ASSERT `the annual holiday pay for` (ahol (Date 1 6 2025) 2 FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) 1000 (Date 25 5 2025) 57200) EQUALS 2200
-- E-051 OWP higher
#ASSERT `the annual holiday pay for` (ahol (Date 1 6 2025) 2 FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) 1200 (Date 25 5 2025) 57200) EQUALS 2400
-- E-052 equal
#ASSERT `the annual holiday pay for` (ahol (Date 1 6 2025) 1 FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) 1000 (Date 25 5 2025) 52000) EQUALS 1000
-- E-053 one day = 0.2 week
#ASSERT `the annual holiday pay for` (ahol (Date 1 6 2025) 0.2 FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) 1000 (Date 25 5 2025) 46800) EQUALS 200
-- E-054 in advance, worked 12 months
#ASSERT `the annual holiday pay for` (ahol (Date 6 1 2025) 1 TRUE (Date 1 1 2024) 900 (Date 31 12 2024) 52000) EQUALS 1000
-- E-055 in advance, 26 weeks exactly
#ASSERT `the annual holiday pay for` (ahol (Date 7 7 2025) 1 TRUE (Date 1 1 2025) 950 (Date 1 7 2025) 26000) EQUALS 1000
-- E-056 26 weeks and 2 days: divisor 27
#ASSERT `the average weekly earnings for the holiday` (ahol (Date 7 7 2025) 1 TRUE (Date 1 1 2025) 900 (Date 3 7 2025) 27000) EQUALS 1000
-- E-057 10 weeks
#ASSERT `the annual holiday pay for` (ahol (Date 17 3 2025) 1 TRUE (Date 1 1 2025) 1000 (Date 11 3 2025) 12000) EQUALS 1200
-- E-060 s 23 8%
#ASSERT `the annual holiday pay owed at the end of` (eoe FALSE 0 1000 0 30000 0 0 0 0) EQUALS 2400
-- E-061 less advance
#ASSERT `the annual holiday pay owed at the end of` (eoe FALSE 0 1000 0 30000 1000 0 0 0) EQUALS 1400
-- E-062 less advance and s 28
#ASSERT `the annual holiday pay owed at the end of` (eoe FALSE 0 1000 0 30000 500 300 0 0) EQUALS 1600
-- E-063 deductions exceed the 8%: nothing payable
#ASSERT `the annual holiday pay owed at the end of` (eoe FALSE 0 1000 0 30000 3000 0 0 0) EQUALS 0
-- E-065 s 24
#ASSERT `the holiday pay under s 24 for` (eoe TRUE 2 1000 54600 0 0 0 0 0) EQUALS 2100
-- E-066
#ASSERT `the holiday pay under s 24 for` (eoe TRUE 4 1200 52000 0 0 0 0 0) EQUALS 4800
-- E-067 all taken
#ASSERT `the holiday pay under s 24 for` (eoe TRUE 0 1200 52000 0 0 0 0 0) EQUALS 0
-- E-068 s 25
#ASSERT `the holiday pay under s 25 for` (eoe TRUE 0 1000 52000 26000 0 0 0 0) EQUALS 2080
-- E-069 ss 24-26 cumulative
#ASSERT `the holiday pay under s 25 for` (eoe TRUE 2 1000 54600 26000 0 0 0 0) EQUALS 2248
#ASSERT `the annual holiday pay owed at the end of` (eoe TRUE 2 1000 54600 26000 0 0 0 0) EQUALS 4348
-- E-070 s 25 less advance
#ASSERT `the annual holiday pay owed at the end of` (eoe TRUE 0 1000 52000 26000 500 0 0 0) EQUALS 1580
-- E-071 s 40(3): ends Fri 19 Dec 2025, 10 working days untaken: 4 public holidays
#ASSERT `the public holidays in the notional holiday after` (Date 19 12 2025) `, working days untaken` 10 `, this year` cal2025 `, next year` cal2026 EQUALS 4
-- E-071b 20 working days untaken, Wellington anniversary Mon 19 Jan 2026 also falls in: 5
#ASSERT `the public holidays in the notional holiday after` (Date 19 12 2025) `, working days untaken` 20 `, this year` cal2025 `, next year` cal2026 EQUALS 5
-- E-071c final pay: ss 24-26 4348 + 4 PH x 200 + 1 untaken alternative holiday x 200
#ASSERT `the final holiday pay for` (eoe TRUE 2 1000 54600 26000 0 0 4 1) EQUALS 5348
-- E-075 to E-077 s 27 timing
#ASSERT `when annual holiday pay is due, agreed to pay in the period:` FALSE `, employment ended:` FALSE `, s 28 applies:` FALSE EQUALS `before the holiday is taken`
#ASSERT `when annual holiday pay is due, agreed to pay in the period:` TRUE `, employment ended:` FALSE `, s 28 applies:` FALSE EQUALS `in the pay for the period in which the holiday is taken`
#ASSERT `when annual holiday pay is due, agreed to pay in the period:` FALSE `, employment ended:` TRUE `, s 28 applies:` FALSE EQUALS `in the pay for the final period of employment`
-- E-080 s 28 fixed term < 12 months at 8%
#ASSERT `annual holiday pay may be paid with the employee's pay` (`Pay-as-you-go arrangement` OF `(a)(i) a fixed-term agreement to work for less than 12 months`, TRUE, TRUE, 8) EQUALS TRUE
-- E-081 7.5%
#ASSERT `annual holiday pay may be paid with the employee's pay` (`Pay-as-you-go arrangement` OF `(a)(i) a fixed-term agreement to work for less than 12 months`, TRUE, TRUE, 7.5) EQUALS FALSE
-- E-083 fixed term exactly 12 months, regular: neither limb
#ASSERT `annual holiday pay may be paid with the employee's pay` (`Pay-as-you-go arrangement` OF `neither`, TRUE, TRUE, 8) EQUALS FALSE
-- E-084 intermittent
#ASSERT `annual holiday pay may be paid with the employee's pay` (`Pay-as-you-go arrangement` OF `(a)(ii) work so intermittent or irregular that 4 weeks' holidays are impracticable`, TRUE, TRUE, 8) EQUALS TRUE
-- E-085 not agreed; E-086 not identifiable
#ASSERT `annual holiday pay may be paid with the employee's pay` (`Pay-as-you-go arrangement` OF `(a)(ii) work so intermittent or irregular that 4 weeks' holidays are impracticable`, FALSE, TRUE, 8) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `annual holiday pay may be paid with the employee's pay` (`Pay-as-you-go arrangement` OF `(a)(ii) work so intermittent or irregular that 4 weeks' holidays are impracticable`, TRUE, FALSE, 8) EQUALS FALSE
-- E-087 fixed term then permanent
#ASSERT `the holiday pay after a fixed term becomes permanent, holiday pay` 4000 `, already received` 1500 EQUALS 2500
-- E-088 PAYG wrongly used, 12 months continued: entitled
#ASSERT `entitled to paid annual holidays despite payments with pay` (`Pay-as-you-go arrangement` OF `neither`, TRUE, TRUE, 8) `, employed 12 months or more:` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- E-090 cash-up 1 week
#ASSERT `the payout for` (pr TRUE 1 0 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 1100
-- E-091 0.6 + 0.4 = 1 week: allowed
#ASSERT `the employer may agree to the payout` (pr TRUE 0.4 0.6 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the payout for` (pr TRUE 0.4 0.6 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 440
-- E-092 0.6 + 0.5 > 1 week
#ASSERT `the employer may agree to the payout` (pr TRUE 0.5 0.6 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
-- E-093 oral
#ASSERT `the employer may agree to the payout` (pr FALSE 1 0 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
-- E-094 s 28E policy
#ASSERT `the employer may agree to the payout` (pr TRUE 1 0 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
-- E-095 employer declines
#ASSERT `the payout for` (pr TRUE 1 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- E-092b a payout above 1 week is never paid
#ASSERT `the payout for` (pr TRUE 1.5 0 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 0
-- E-096 s 28B(2)
#ASSERT `the entitlement remains after a payout, requested:` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the entitlement remains after a payout, requested:` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- E-100 second closedown in 12 months
#ASSERT `the employer may require the closedown` (cd (Date 1 12 2025) TRUE TRUE 2 3 FALSE 0 0) EQUALS FALSE
-- E-101 notice 8 Dec for 22 Dec = 14 days: valid; 9 Dec: invalid
#ASSERT `the employer may require the closedown` (cd (Date 8 12 2025) FALSE TRUE 2 3 FALSE 0 0) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the employer may require the closedown` (cd (Date 9 12 2025) FALSE TRUE 2 3 FALSE 0 0) EQUALS FALSE
-- E-102 s 33 entitled, 2 weeks of 3 available
#ASSERT (`the closedown position for` (cd (Date 1 12 2025) FALSE TRUE 2 3 FALSE 0 0))'s `weeks taken as annual holidays` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT (`the closedown position for` (cd (Date 1 12 2025) FALSE TRUE 2 3 FALSE 0 0))'s `holiday pay for the closedown` EQUALS 2000
-- E-103 s 33(3) only 1 week available, no agreement
#ASSERT (`the closedown position for` (cd (Date 1 12 2025) FALSE TRUE 2 1 FALSE 0 0))'s `weeks taken as annual holidays` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT (`the closedown position for` (cd (Date 1 12 2025) FALSE TRUE 2 1 FALSE 0 0))'s `weeks taken as annual holidays in advance` EQUALS 0
-- E-104 s 34 not entitled: 8% of 20000, less 200 advance
#ASSERT (`the closedown position for` (cd (Date 1 12 2025) FALSE FALSE 2 0 FALSE 20000 0))'s `holiday pay for the closedown` EQUALS 1600
#ASSERT (`the closedown position for` (cd (Date 1 12 2025) FALSE FALSE 2 0 FALSE 20000 200))'s `holiday pay for the closedown` EQUALS 1400
-- E-105 s 35 restart
#ASSERT (`the closedown position for` (cd (Date 1 12 2025) FALSE FALSE 2 0 FALSE 20000 0))'s `the 12 months restart at the closedown (s 35)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the 12 months restart, under s 35, on` (Date 22 12 2025) `, nominated` NOTHING EQUALS Date 22 12 2025
#ASSERT `the day the employee becomes entitled to annual holidays, 12 months from` (Date 22 12 2025) `, absences` EMPTY EQUALS Date 22 12 2026
-- E-106 first anniversary is the closedown's first day: entitled at commencement
#ASSERT `the day the employee becomes entitled to annual holidays, 12 months from` (Date 22 12 2024) `, absences` EMPTY EQUALS Date 22 12 2025
-- E-110 to E-114 ss 36-39
#ASSERT `how the time may be taken under ss 36 to 39` `s 36 sick or injured, or a spouse, partner or dependant is, during annual holidays` EQUALS `as sick leave, if the employer agrees`
#ASSERT `how the time may be taken under ss 36 to 39` `s 37 a bereavement during annual holidays` EQUALS `as bereavement leave, which the employer must allow`
#ASSERT `how the time may be taken under ss 36 to 39` `s 37A family violence leave becomes available during annual holidays` EQUALS `as family violence leave, which the employer must allow`
#ASSERT `how the time may be taken under ss 36 to 39` `s 38 any of these before scheduled annual holidays` EQUALS `as sick, bereavement or family violence leave, which the employer must allow`
#ASSERT `how the time may be taken under ss 36 to 39` `s 39 sick, bereavement or family violence leave exhausted` EQUALS `not as annual holidays unless the employer agrees to the employee's request`
-- E-115 s 40(1)
#ASSERT `the days of annual holidays used, working days in the holiday` 10 `, public holidays on them` 2 EQUALS 8

§ `3. Public holidays`

-- E-121 to E-124 Easter
#ASSERT `Easter Sunday in` 2026 EQUALS Date 5 4 2026
#ASSERT `the day` (`Good Friday`) `is treated as falling on, calendar` cal2026 EQUALS Date 3 4 2026
#ASSERT `the day` (`Easter Monday`) `is treated as falling on, calendar` cal2026 EQUALS Date 6 4 2026
#ASSERT `the day` (`Good Friday`) `is treated as falling on, calendar` cal2025 EQUALS Date 18 4 2025
#ASSERT `the day` (`Easter Monday`) `is treated as falling on, calendar` cal2025 EQUALS Date 21 4 2025
#ASSERT `the day` (`Good Friday`) `is treated as falling on, calendar` cal2024 EQUALS Date 29 3 2024
#ASSERT `the day` (`Easter Monday`) `is treated as falling on, calendar` cal2024 EQUALS Date 1 4 2024
#ASSERT `the day` (`Good Friday`) `is treated as falling on, calendar` cal2027 EQUALS Date 26 3 2027
#ASSERT `the day` (`Easter Monday`) `is treated as falling on, calendar` cal2027 EQUALS Date 29 3 2027
#ASSERT `Easter Sunday in` 2038 EQUALS Date 25 4 2038
-- E-125 Sovereign's birthday
#ASSERT `the day` (`the Sovereign's birthday`) `is treated as falling on, calendar` cal2026 EQUALS Date 1 6 2026
#ASSERT `the day` (`the Sovereign's birthday`) `is treated as falling on, calendar` cal2025 EQUALS Date 2 6 2025
#ASSERT `the day` (`the Sovereign's birthday`) `is treated as falling on, calendar` cal2027 EQUALS Date 7 6 2027
